  "tagline": "EnterpriseDB's PostgreSQL with deep Oracle compatibility: PL/SQL packages, DBMS_* and TDE.",
  "description": "EDB Postgres Advanced Server (EPAS) is EnterpriseDB's commercial distribution of PostgreSQL, built to run Oracle applications with minimal rewriting. On top of each upstream major version it adds Oracle-compatible PL/SQL, packages, synonyms, hierarchical queries, a large set of DBMS_* and UTL_* built-ins, Oracle-style partitioning syntax, resource management, auditing and transparent data encryption. It is the core of EDB's Postgres AI platform and is available self-managed, on Kubernetes via EDB's CloudNativePG-based operator, and as a managed cloud service. It is the most mature path off Oracle within the Postgres world, at the cost of a proprietary subscription.",
